{% set p1 %}{% t %}A token lets something that is not a browser talk to your workspace: your CRM, an agent you are building, a script. Read a company, start a pitch, read a saved one, record an outcome, take a copy out.{% endt %}{% endset %}
{% set p2 %}{% t %}You tick what a token may do when you mint it, and it never gains a scope later. It expires when you say. The secret is shown once; losing it costs one revoke and one mint.{% endt %}{% endset %}
{% set p3 %}{% t %}Only the workspace's owner can mint one, because a token acts as the whole workspace with nobody watching. The card names each token, who minted it and when it expires.{% endt %}{% endset %}
{% set s1 %}{% t %}Open <strong>Connect your apps → Your own agent → New token</strong> in your workspace settings.{% endt %}{% endset %}
{% set s2 %}{% t %}Label it with what will hold it, tick what it may do, set when it expires, press <strong>Mint</strong>.{% endt %}{% endset %}
{% set s3 %}{% t %}Copy the secret now; nothing can show it again. <strong>Copy setup for your agent</strong> gives your own Claude the whole of it.{% endt %}{% endset %}

